  "source_inspection": {
    "java": [
      "PSystemBuilder tries generic @startuml factories in registration order: SequenceDiagramFactory, then ClassDiagramFactory, then DescriptionDiagramFactory. The first complete successful factory wins.",
      "PSystemCommandFactory rejects a candidate factory as soon as no command matches a line, an execution error occurs, or the diagram finishes incomplete.",
      "ClassDiagramFactory accepts quoted shared containers through CommandPackageWithUSymbol and class-family declarations through CommandCreateClass and CommandCreateClassMultilines.",
      "CommandCreateElementFull2 reuses CommandCreateElementFull.ALL_TYPES, so without allowmixing it rejects normal-keyword description leaves broadly, not just component leaves."
    ],
    "rust": [
      "Commit 1f243f89 introduces class_factory_viable, but the invalidating evidence is only has_class_factory_incompatible_component_leaf set by trimmed.starts_with(\"component \") without braces.",
      "Bare, inline-empty, and multiline entity declarations still set has_entity_class_factory_decl and has_class_factory_decl, and quoted shared-container promotion uses class_factory_viable to decide whether CLASS outranks DESCRIPTION.",
      "Nothing in detect_uml_subtype marks database, artifact, cloud, frame, node, queue, boundary, control, collections, or bracket component leaves as class-factory-incompatible even though Java routes those through CommandCreateElementFull2 under the same allowmixing gate."
    ],
    "fixture_shaping_search": "No mechanism name, held-out filename stem, or held-out diagram text appeared in shipping crate logic.",
